.TH MICROPOLIS 6 "August 2026" "Micropolis" "Games Manual"
.SH NAME
micropolis \- run the Micropolis city simulation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B micropolis
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B micropolis
starts a small HTTP server bound exclusively to the IPv4 loopback address
and serves the packaged Micropolis web application.  It then opens the
application in the user's default browser using
.BR xdg-open (1).
.PP
The default port is stable so browser-managed game settings and saved state
remain associated with the same origin between launches.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --no-browser
Start the local server without opening a browser.
.TP
.BI --port " PORT"
Listen on PORT instead of the default port 48080.  Port 0 requests an
ephemeral port.  Changing ports changes the browser origin and can therefore
make browser-stored settings or saved state appear separate.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MICROPOLIS_WEB_ROOT
Override the directory from which the packaged web tree is served.  This is
primarily intended for package testing.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/micropolis/web/MicropolisCore
Packaged static Micropolis application.
.SH SECURITY
The built-in HTTP server binds only to 127.0.0.1 and is not exposed on
external network interfaces.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR xdg-open (1)
